{"name":"Yellow Mandarin","hex":"#d28034","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"mandarin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high government bureaucrat of the Chinese Empire. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A pedantic or elitist bureaucrat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or reminiscent of mandarins; deliberately superior or complex; esoteric, highbrow, obscurantist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yellow mandarin","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow mandarin is a common name for several plants and may refer to:"},{"items":["Prosartes lanuginosa","Prosartes maculata"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_mandarin","wikidata":"Q25036271"},{"title":"Mandarin (character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mandarin is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. He is the archenemy of Iron Man. The character was created by Stan Lee and designed by Don Heck, first appearing in Tales of Suspense #50. The character is described as being born in China before the Communist revolution to a wealthy Chinese father and an English aristocratic mother, both of whom died when he was young. He is characterized as a megalomaniac, attempting to conquer the world on several occasions, yet also possessing a strong sense of honor. The Mandarin is portrayed as a genius scientist and a skilled martial artist. However, his primary sources of power are 10 rings that he adapted from the alien technology of a crashed spaceship. Each ring has a different power and is worn on a specific finger. Though his primary obsession is Iron Man, given his high status as a supervillain, he has also come into conflict with Thor, Hulk, Shang-Chi, and other superheroes in the Marvel Universe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Mandarin_%28Marvel_Comics_character_circa_2011%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandarin_(character)","wikidata":"Q2417914"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png/250px-Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png/250px-Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cover of Tales of Suspense #50 (Feb. 1964), the first appearance of the Mandarin, art by Jack Kirby","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATales_of_Suspense_(1959)_-50.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/1280px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ben Kingsley at the 2014 San Diego Comic-Con","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABen_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tony Leung in 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATony_Leung_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi